1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,376
The consequences were emotional and, at the core, simple.

2
00:00:04,376 --> 00:00:13,580
The last question in the survey asked what a family is for, and the answers exposed a vacuum where a definition should have been.

3
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:23,349
A prince, a princess, and a philosopher gave the same reply: for holding what cannot be held anywhere else.

4
00:00:23,349 --> 00:00:27,738
The appearance of a stranger at the door changed the morning.

5
00:00:27,738 --> 00:00:38,107
A porter, a waiter, and a fireman came to the residence to repair the rail; a hunter in a blue coat brought a rabbit for the infant next door.

6
00:00:38,107 --> 00:00:42,166
“Anybody could have done it,” the tailor said.

7
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:44,991
“Nobody did.”

8
00:00:44,991 --> 00:00:50,206
The intention of the donor was good, and the delivery was terrible.

9
00:00:50,206 --> 00:00:59,704
They received a melon, a vacuum cleaner, and a bench with a mysterious inscription from an ancestor of the family of the butcher.

10
00:00:59,704 --> 00:01:07,518
A second parcel arrived for him the same afternoon, addressed to the wrong man and opened by everyone.

11
00:01:07,518 --> 00:01:11,778
“They will dismiss it as charming,” Maya said.

12
00:01:11,778 --> 00:01:16,387
“That is the exception, not the rule.”

13
00:01:16,387 --> 00:01:21,736
He was away when the kiss happened, and he had to hear of it from her.

14
00:01:21,736 --> 00:01:40,145
“You will say I am like the man in the old story,” she said, “and I am not sure that I am not.” The chilly answer was that the germ of the quarrel had been there since the first week, and he had to be sure of that before he could say it aloud.

15
00:01:40,145 --> 00:01:47,639
Dad was living in a small flat around the corner, and it had taken real talent to be so ordinary.

16
00:01:47,639 --> 00:02:01,592
The imaginative descendant of a blond Homo sapiens and a diligent tailor wrote a parade of small substitutions: a bench for a bed, a rabbit for a rabbit, a question for a question.

17
00:02:01,592 --> 00:02:11,400
The hatred between the two families had not disappeared; it had simply gone back to being what it had been at the beginning — a habit they could lose.

18
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:29,308
The tailor had mended the same coat three times, and the butcher had sold him the same cut of meat for twenty years; neither of them had ever said the word hatred aloud, and that silence, too, was a kind of inheritance.
